The problem states that Rachel scores 9 points for each treasure she finds. She found 5 treasures on the first level and 2 on the second. 

First, calculate the points from the first level:  
$ 5 \text{ treasures} \times 9 \text{ points/treasure} = 45 \text{ points} $

Next, calculate the points from the second level:  
$ 2 \text{ treasures} \times 9 \text{ points/treasure} = 18 \text{ points} $

Add the points from both levels:  
$ 45 \text{ points} + 18 \text{ points} = 63 \text{ points} $

Thus, Rachel's total score is $\boxed{63}$.  
