The problem involves determining how many customers left a tip after initially serving 26 customers and adding another 27 during the lunch rush.

1. Calculate the **total number of customers**:
   $$
   26 \ (\text{initial}) + 27 \ (\text{added}) = 53 \ (\text{total customers})
   $$

2. Subtract the number of customers **who didn’t leave a tip**:
   $$
   53 \ (\text{total}) - 27 \ (\text{no tip}) = 26 \ (\text{with tip})
   $$

Thus, the number of customers who left a tip is:
